::JOUR_U05_L06_GP_Q01::[MLA.JOUR.ETH.02] Source: Multimedia Spirit Week Package. Project: A student media team is creating a multimedia package about Spirit Week for the school website. Package Parts: A short article, a 20-second recap video, a photo gallery, and a captioned quote card from the student council president. Team Conflict: The video editor wants fast music and quick cuts. The reporter wants slower pacing so the quote is clear. The photo editor wants the gallery first because the photos are strong. The web editor says the package needs a consistent tone, accurate captions, and a logical order for readers. Audience: Students, families, and staff who want a clear recap of the week. Collaboration Need: The team must compromise respectfully, maintain a cohesive package, use accurate visuals, and prepare publication-ready work. Question 1: Which compromise best protects the video and quote? {
